  "observations": [
    "Psi CUDA uses a16x16 shared-memory FP32 SGEMM or cuBLAS SGEMM and host copies each call; no Hopper WGMMA/NVFP4 expert kernel in reviewed backend.",
    "Psi Metal notes describe vectorization, register tiles and padding; vendor/shape/precision differ from H200. Ternary-weight conversion is incompatible with task weight precision.",
    "Shohin uses PyTorch SDPA, BF16 autocast, torch.compile and DDP; its reported training throughput does not identify a Muse kernel submission.",
